@startuml
title Step 9+ : NSSMF allocatNSSI operation for each domain (5G Core, Transport and RAN)

participant "Service Order\nManagement" as SOM #blue
participant "Service Catalog\nManagement" as SCM #blue
participant "Service Inventory" as SI #blue
participant "Event Mgt" as EventMgt #grey
participant "Resource Order\nManagement" as ROM #blue

SOM -> SOM : 1 <<3GPP>> allocateNSSI (SliceProfile with attribute list)

SOM -> SI : 2 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nGET /service
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 3 **TMF638** 201 RFS (Slice Profile RFS, Slice RFS, Slice Subnet RFS)
deactivate SI

SOM -> SCM : 4 **TMF633 Service Catalog Management**\nGET /serviceSpecification (RFS Specification)
activate SCM
SCM --> SOM : 5 **TMF633** 200 RFS Specification
deactivate SCM

note over SOM
  a.Qualitative design based on functional and performance requirements as per slice profile
  b.Quantitative design - Topology, Placement, and Resource Allocation Requirements
end note

SOM -> SI : 6 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPATCH /service\n(state="designed")
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 7 **TMF638** 201 RFS
deactivate SI

note over SOM : Network Slice Subnet RFS state marked as designed

ref over SOM
  modifyNSSI procedure
end ref

SOM -> SOM : 8 Create NSSI

SOM -> SI : 9 **TMF638 Service Inventory Management**\nPOST /service\n(state="reserved")
activate SI
SI --> SOM : 10 **TMF638** 201 RFS
deactivate SI

note over SOM
  a. prepare dependencies
  b. prepare onnectivity demands
  c. prepare service automation workflow
end note

SOM -> SOM : 11 Prepare resourceOrderItems

SOM -> ROM : 12 **TMF652 Resource Order Management**\nPOST /resourceOrder
activate ROM
ROM -> ROM : 13 validate resourceOrder
ROM --> SOM : 14 **TMF652** 201 resourceOrder (state="acknowledged")
deactivate ROM

note over ROM : Refer to "NSSI Level NFV Operation - For Virtualized Network Functions" diagram 5.5.2.2
note over SOM : Refer to "NSSI Constituent Provisioning" diagram 5.5.2.3

@enduml
